|Main Details=Pairagrim are highly coordinated aerial predators. Each head has a distinct role—one focuses on flight and maneuvering, while the other scans for prey—allowing them to navigate dense forests at high speed and perform sharp turns, dives, and other advanced aerial maneuvers. They fly with minimal noise and strike only when success is assured. Pairagrim are solitary hunters outside of nesting season and typically raise small clutches of one to three chicks. Though more serious and calculating than their juvenile form, they can still form strong bonds with trainers. The two heads possess separate minds but remain closely synchronized, rarely disagreeing.
